 be available to the public, on request, by fax or mail. 24. (1) The summary shall : (a)subject to subsection (3), set out the source and nature, but not the value, of the income, assets and liabilities referred to in the Member’s statement filed under section 20;(b) identify any contracts or subcontracts referred to in paragraph 21(1)(c) and describe their subject-matter and nature;(c) list the names of any affiliated corporations referred to in that statement; (d) include a copy of any statements of disclosure filed by the Member under subsections 14(3), 15(1) and 21(3); (e) list the positions and corporations, trade or professional associations and trade unions disclosed under paragraph 21(1)(e); and (f) list any trusts disclosed under paragraph 21(1)(b.1). Richard Bragdon · Member of Parliament Declaration type Disclosure Summaries (Code) Disclosure date January 16, 2026 Regime Conflict of Interest Code for Members of the House of Commons Description Other Sources of IncomeLast 12 months: - Professional income from Exit RealtyNext 12 months: - Professional income from Exit RealtyLiabilities- Mortgage and home equity line of credit with the Royal Bank of Canada, with spouse- Line of credit with Scotiabank, with spouse- Vehicle loan with Kia Financing, with spouse- Vehicle loan with Mitsubishi Motors Financial Services, with spouseSpouse's/Common-Law Partner's source(s) of incomeLast 12 months:- Employment income from the New Brunswick Anglophone West School DistrictNext 12 months:- Employment income from the New Brunswick Anglophone West School District Disclosed on January 16, 2026","url":"https://www.ethicscanada.ca/en/public-registry/Details?declarationId=ed03fed5-2bf2-f011-81a0-001dd8b72449"}],"other":[]},"lobbying":{"total":212,"first":"2019-12-09","last":"2026-10-07","byYear":{"2019":2,"2020":25,"2021":28,"2022":25,"2023":13,"2024":33,"2025":60,"2026":26},"topSubjects":[["Environment",38],["Health",26],["Agriculture",23],["Fisheries",20],["Budget",17],["Int